WEBVTT

00:06.600 --> 00:08.590
Hey, what's...

00:09.520 --> 00:10.990
What's Pas up to?

00:11.930 --> 00:14.110
Working on some kind of sample sweet...

00:14.770 --> 00:16.560
made by whisking egg whites.

00:17.050 --> 00:19.820
He's been at it... all day!

00:21.240 --> 00:23.300
He's been doing that same motion all day?

00:24.250 --> 00:29.020
<b>Bulge</b>

00:25.200 --> 00:26.580
Not a bad way...

00:26.580 --> 00:28.850
...of building muscle, I'd wager.

00:29.230 --> 00:30.660
You'd think that, right?

00:32.480 --> 00:33.550
Wh-What?!

00:33.550 --> 00:36.680
No muscle has formed, 
even after all that labor?!

00:38.710 --> 00:42.140
You're clearly shocked 
by my slim, delicate arm.

00:42.490 --> 00:43.480
It's because...

00:44.350 --> 00:46.800
What you develop through whisking eggs

00:46.800 --> 00:48.610
is STMF!

00:48.610 --> 00:50.290
"Small-to-medium fowl"?

00:50.860 --> 00:53.780
"Slow-twitch muscle fibers."

00:53.780 --> 00:58.070
By exposing my arms to prolonged 
low-burden exercise,

00:58.070 --> 01:03.110
I develop lithe and firm arms 
without bulging muscles!

01:04.020 --> 01:05.030
But more importantly,

01:05.030 --> 01:08.330
the crucial factor in muscle 
development is diet!

01:11.050 --> 01:14.890
Most calories from sweets come 
from carbohydrates and fat,

01:14.890 --> 01:17.130
with very low protein values,

01:17.130 --> 01:18.980
so they don't build muscle!

01:18.980 --> 01:21.970
You need to eat real food!

01:24.250 --> 01:29.270
<i>This is the tale of a genius patissier 
who died before his time,</i>

01:29.270 --> 01:33.280
<i>and was reincarnated as the son 
of a poor noble in another world</i>

01:33.590 --> 01:36.620
<i>to pursue a world full 
of desserts and smiles.</i>

01:37.530 --> 01:42.290
<i>It's a tale that is at once cold 
and unsparing, and syrupy sweet.</i>

01:43.640 --> 01:50.080
<i>His dream is to create this 
world's very own land of sweets!</i>

01:58.010 --> 02:00.590
<b>Sweet Reincarnation</b>

03:22.490 --> 03:27.140
<b>Reinforcements and a Bittersweet First Deployment</b>

03:23.360 --> 03:25.430
War has begun.

03:27.140 --> 03:32.600
It started between Hubarek's lands in 
the east and their neighbor, Lutoroute.

03:34.560 --> 03:37.020
<b>Lutoroute War Camp</b>

03:37.510 --> 03:39.240
According to reports,

03:39.240 --> 03:42.490
there's been no word yet of 
reinforcements from the duke's estate

03:42.490 --> 03:44.250
in the royal capital.

03:45.060 --> 03:46.660
Just as I thought.

03:47.040 --> 03:51.120
The moment they heard the false rumor 
that our army was 30,000 strong,

03:51.400 --> 03:55.200
Hubarek would have requested 
aid from Kadlecek.

03:55.200 --> 03:58.110
The fact that there's been 
no action there means...

03:58.110 --> 03:59.930
Either the duke turned him down,

03:59.930 --> 04:04.300
or the Hubareks withdrew 
their request for aid.

04:04.300 --> 04:05.930
It'll be the latter.

04:05.930 --> 04:08.350
The minute he learned we 
have only ten thousand,

04:08.350 --> 04:12.330
he'd want to handle us himself to save face.

04:12.660 --> 04:16.070
He won't want large-scale 
participation by the ducal house.

04:16.520 --> 04:20.070
I doubt the duke will appreciate that.

04:20.070 --> 04:22.490
We can assume it was a source of conflict.

04:25.330 --> 04:27.190
Just watch me, Hubarek.

04:27.190 --> 04:29.550
I'll settle this long-standing 
grudge between us...

04:29.950 --> 04:31.910
with your destruction!

04:32.420 --> 04:33.530
Milord!

04:34.080 --> 04:36.560
I've received word that the daughter's fiancé

04:36.560 --> 04:39.380
is currently stationed in the margravate.

04:41.690 --> 04:42.730
Oh?

04:42.730 --> 04:45.110
The duke's grandson, you mean?

04:53.440 --> 04:54.580
Pas!

04:55.700 --> 04:57.900
Is something the matter?

04:59.940 --> 05:02.380
You seemed a bit lost in thought.

05:02.780 --> 05:05.450
Oh, no, I'm just fine!

05:05.820 --> 05:09.580
Were you thinking about the war?

05:11.770 --> 05:16.000
I heard that war was breaking out 
between my homeland and its neighbor...

05:17.820 --> 05:18.920
I...

05:20.920 --> 05:25.370
I believe we're thinking the same thing.

05:26.310 --> 05:30.570
War is a foolish thing. 
Why do they have to fight?

05:33.450 --> 05:38.600
Instead of waging war, they could 
be making delicious sweets...

05:38.970 --> 05:41.570
If they could lose themselves 
in it the way that you do,

05:42.390 --> 05:46.460
and eat the finished desserts with a smile...

05:48.280 --> 05:54.010
Then everyone in the world 
could be happy and joyous!

05:57.610 --> 05:59.270
I feel the same way.

06:03.200 --> 06:06.400
Sweets make everyone happy!

06:06.810 --> 06:09.010
Behind every smile, there's a sweet!

06:09.010 --> 06:11.690
The road to happiness is paved with sweets!

06:11.690 --> 06:12.930
That's the right answer!

06:14.720 --> 06:15.720
Yes!

06:19.290 --> 06:20.440
Oh, right!

06:20.810 --> 06:23.850
The merchant's going to 
deliver the goats today.

06:23.850 --> 06:24.770
Goats?

06:24.770 --> 06:30.450
Cheesecake made from goat's 
milk is rich and delicious!

06:30.450 --> 06:31.950
Cheesecake?

06:31.950 --> 06:33.700
I'd love to try that!

06:33.700 --> 06:36.910
Right? You can set your hopes high, then!

06:37.210 --> 06:38.010
I will!

06:40.900 --> 06:43.050
Someone swiped the goats?!

06:43.050 --> 06:44.530
Explain this at once!

06:45.300 --> 06:46.810
Well, actually...

06:46.810 --> 06:51.500
"Before I could bring them here, 
another noble bought them all up,"

06:51.500 --> 06:53.400
would be more precise.

06:53.400 --> 06:55.310
That's still basically swiping them!

06:56.490 --> 06:59.880
To force a person to sell 
something under threat

06:59.880 --> 07:02.070
isn't much different from stealing.

07:03.190 --> 07:05.090
I'm so sorry!

07:05.090 --> 07:08.900
I tried to explain that they 
already had a buyer, but...

07:09.190 --> 07:11.180
They said the circumstances were dire,

07:11.180 --> 07:14.400
and they'd kill me if I 
didn't hand over the goats!

07:14.400 --> 07:16.320
I didn't have a choice...

07:16.750 --> 07:18.310
I understand.

07:18.310 --> 07:21.400
Thank you for coming in person to explain.

07:21.400 --> 07:23.880
So? Who'd you sell them to?

07:24.450 --> 07:26.930
Baron Lunzvage.

07:26.930 --> 07:31.370
Ah, the one famous for picking 
on newer noble families...

07:31.800 --> 07:35.570
Having a familial connection to 
a powerful noble would help us

07:35.570 --> 07:38.330
to lodge a complaint, but...

07:40.090 --> 07:44.610
But the engagement to House Hubarek 
has not yet been formalized.

07:44.920 --> 07:48.730
It would be difficult to ask 
the margrave to intervene.

07:49.590 --> 07:53.470
Besides, this is likely a consequence 
of the conflict between

07:53.470 --> 07:55.720
the houses of Hubarek and Lutoroute.

07:56.430 --> 07:59.780
Complaining about the shockwaves from 
that won't earn us much sympathy.

07:59.780 --> 08:02.480
So we basically just have to suck it up?

08:02.480 --> 08:05.280
We only got word of the 
war three days ago, too.

08:05.280 --> 08:08.910
Hard to believe it's already affecting us...

08:08.910 --> 08:11.440
It's gotta be a pretty big conflict,

08:11.440 --> 08:14.040
and we're all connected by trade.

08:14.040 --> 08:17.330
Even distant regions will be 
at least somewhat affected.

08:17.330 --> 08:19.180
Is this a trial, then?

08:19.930 --> 08:23.020
Baron, heron, whatever he is...

08:23.370 --> 08:24.650
Pas?

08:25.870 --> 08:29.150
Anyone who gets in the way of my fun

08:29.150 --> 08:31.360
must be purged from the face of this world!

08:31.360 --> 08:35.620
We mustn't permit this kind of tyranny! 
Morteln's pride can't survive it!

08:35.620 --> 08:36.490
What's wrong, kid?

08:36.490 --> 08:37.310
Calm down!

08:37.310 --> 08:38.980
How can I be calm?!

08:38.980 --> 08:42.930
I'm gonna march right up to that baron 
guy and give him a piece of my mind!

08:42.930 --> 08:43.710
Pas!

08:44.290 --> 08:46.180
You need to calm down.

08:46.180 --> 08:47.210
But Father—

08:47.210 --> 08:48.920
Lands are at war.

08:48.920 --> 08:53.130
Every fief is going to 
need supplies, especially food.

08:53.850 --> 08:57.650
And the Lunzvage Barony is closer 
to the front lines than ours.

08:58.620 --> 09:02.220
It's natural that they'd have 
a pressing need for food.

09:02.220 --> 09:04.710
Besides, he didn't steal the goats.

09:04.710 --> 09:06.870
He still paid for them.

09:07.360 --> 09:10.400
I'm sorry you lost your chance to buy them,

09:10.400 --> 09:13.370
but you're the only one who's 
actually been harmed by that.

09:13.370 --> 09:14.970
You have to acknowledge that.

09:14.970 --> 09:16.430
You're right.

09:16.430 --> 09:16.880
But—

09:16.880 --> 09:18.380
So even if you went to get them back,

09:18.380 --> 09:23.080
he'd just use the war as 
an excuse to dismiss you.

09:25.640 --> 09:27.410
I understand that you're frustrated,

09:27.410 --> 09:29.700
but you need to accept reality.

09:30.400 --> 09:32.230
But I really need those goats!

09:32.230 --> 09:36.010
Once the conflict is settled, 
you'll get a chance to negotiate.

09:36.270 --> 09:37.970
Though it won't be easy.

09:40.540 --> 09:42.000
Cheesecake?

09:42.000 --> 09:43.770
I'd love to try that!

09:44.140 --> 09:45.970
<i>Why must people go to war?</i>

09:47.850 --> 09:50.140
<i>It doesn't make anyone happy!</i>

09:50.530 --> 09:52.500
Say, I've got an idea!

09:53.110 --> 09:57.570
A way to get your pick 
of supplies, even during war.

09:59.370 --> 10:01.280
That's it! Reinforcements!

10:01.940 --> 10:04.400
If we join the war as reinforcements,

10:04.400 --> 10:07.520
we can assert priority 
selection of provisions!

10:07.520 --> 10:08.500
Exactly!

10:08.790 --> 10:12.140
Baron Lunzvage is famous 
for his miserly ways.

10:12.140 --> 10:14.890
I doubt he's offering much in the way of aid.

10:14.890 --> 10:17.220
But if we join the reinforcement ourselves,

10:17.220 --> 10:20.100
it could give us a leg up on him.

10:21.680 --> 10:25.110
And since Pas and Licorice are engaged,

10:25.110 --> 10:28.620
we have a reason to side with Hubarek.

10:28.620 --> 10:29.830
I've decided.

10:31.110 --> 10:34.020
Watch me, Baron Lunzvage!

10:34.610 --> 10:35.910
Those goats...

10:36.360 --> 10:38.970
are my goats!

10:41.740 --> 10:44.030
Pas is the adjutant,

10:44.030 --> 10:47.000
and the lord is the commander?

10:47.530 --> 10:49.730
The retainers are my dad and Nicolo.

10:49.730 --> 10:52.360
I hope that newbie can handle the job...

10:54.940 --> 10:57.900
That, plus eight footsoldiers 
recruited from our villages.

10:58.790 --> 11:00.630
Twelve in all.

11:01.390 --> 11:04.180
Damn it! I wanted to go, too!

11:04.180 --> 11:06.980
You would've just been a burden.

11:06.980 --> 11:08.110
What was that?!

11:08.760 --> 11:10.860
We've got an important job, too.

11:10.860 --> 11:13.650
Protecting the fief while 
our suzerain's gone.

11:13.650 --> 11:15.860
I know that, Dad!

11:16.110 --> 11:20.990
But to make all their preparations 
and leave in one day...

11:20.990 --> 11:25.350
The boss and the kid are always 
prepared for an emergency.

11:25.350 --> 11:27.780
They believe in being ready for anything!

11:27.780 --> 11:31.080
There's nothing to worry about, Licorice.

11:31.080 --> 11:32.410
I know...

11:36.460 --> 11:37.760
<i>Sorry, Licorice,</i>

11:38.110 --> 11:40.060
<i>for going off to the front myself.</i>

11:40.670 --> 11:42.420
<i>But I'm doing it for sweets...</i>

11:42.420 --> 11:45.470
<i>Rather, to right a wrong!</i>

11:46.700 --> 11:48.430
<i>Once I get my goats back,</i>

11:48.430 --> 11:51.130
<i>I'll make lots of delicious desserts!</i>

12:01.610 --> 12:03.020
So charming...

12:03.020 --> 12:05.400
You have the real me right here!

12:05.400 --> 12:07.770
How can you be preoccupied with a picture?!

12:07.770 --> 12:09.270
I-I wasn't!

12:09.270 --> 12:11.500
It's just, the real you is so charming,

12:11.500 --> 12:13.540
I feel like I have to prepare myself.

12:13.850 --> 12:15.000
My!

12:19.670 --> 12:22.600
<i>Yeah, Petra really is charming...</i>

12:25.390 --> 12:26.880
Well done!

12:27.640 --> 12:31.600
That was a great cover story you 
pulled out of thin air, Lord Squale.

12:31.840 --> 12:33.180
It wasn't a cover story!

12:33.180 --> 12:34.560
I meant it! I don't—

12:34.560 --> 12:38.060
Father, don't tease Lord Squale!

12:38.060 --> 12:39.800
Oh, sorry.

12:39.800 --> 12:41.770
Please excuse him, Lord Squale.

12:41.770 --> 12:43.290
No offense taken.

12:43.290 --> 12:44.840
Shall we take a walk?

12:44.840 --> 12:45.930
Milord!

12:46.280 --> 12:49.990
Lutoroute's main force is on the march!

12:50.220 --> 12:50.950
What?!

12:51.630 --> 12:53.660
They number just over ten thousand!

12:53.660 --> 12:55.090
Ten thousand?

12:55.660 --> 12:59.510
So the original report of 
thirty thousand was falsified.

12:59.510 --> 13:03.040
We should be able to handle them 
with our forces alone, then.

13:04.090 --> 13:06.230
Lord Squale, you heard the man.

13:06.230 --> 13:06.950
Sir!

13:07.680 --> 13:11.310
I'd like to put you on 
the front line defenses.

13:12.550 --> 13:15.290
No! With our army alone?!

13:15.290 --> 13:18.980
Petra, I know what I'm doing.

13:18.980 --> 13:20.090
But...

13:24.840 --> 13:25.580
My lord!

13:26.360 --> 13:29.380
Thank you for gifting me my first campaign.

13:29.380 --> 13:31.160
I'll set out at once!

13:31.160 --> 13:32.080
Good.

13:32.360 --> 13:33.540
See to it!

13:33.540 --> 13:34.410
Sir.

13:34.410 --> 13:35.830
Lord Squale...

13:35.830 --> 13:36.890
Don't worry.

13:36.890 --> 13:39.500
I will protect your father's lands.

13:42.460 --> 13:44.920
<b>Lutoroute War Camp</b>

13:43.980 --> 13:44.920
Reporting in!

13:45.370 --> 13:49.890
Part of the advance unit has arrived 
near the border and formed rank!

13:50.110 --> 13:51.110
Excellent work.

13:51.110 --> 13:52.100
Milord.

13:52.510 --> 13:55.210
Our forces are showing signs of fatigue,

13:55.210 --> 13:58.810
and the Hubarek army is 
steadily growing their ranks.

13:59.090 --> 14:01.150
We could end up at a disadvantage.

14:02.120 --> 14:06.020
You think I didn't account for that?

14:06.020 --> 14:07.280
Certainly not, milord...

14:08.150 --> 14:12.490
My real goal here is to tear 
Hubarek and Kadlecek apart.

14:12.490 --> 14:15.210
The margrave and the duke?

14:16.470 --> 14:19.660
Kadlecek's heir is stationed 
at House Hubarek.

14:19.660 --> 14:21.750
He's never been in a real battle before.

14:22.110 --> 14:25.770
Hubarek likely wants to grant 
him his first campaign,

14:25.770 --> 14:30.360
but he can't just go throwing a 
dignitary's grandson into jeopardy.

14:30.360 --> 14:33.580
If you expect an easy battle, though,

14:33.580 --> 14:35.510
it's a perfect chance for a first deployment.

14:35.510 --> 14:40.150
And if he gives him a win, 
he'll have Kadlecek's gratitude.

14:40.420 --> 14:42.710
That's why I'm going to lure him out

14:42.710 --> 14:45.110
to a place where I can easily finish him.

14:48.040 --> 14:50.240
The girl will lose her fiancé.

14:50.450 --> 14:53.920
Kadlecek will be furious 
and cut ties with him.

14:53.920 --> 14:58.460
Hubarek will be isolated, his attempt 
to expand his forces up in smoke.

14:58.460 --> 15:01.680
And while he's still reeling from that,
 I'll mount our all-out attack.

15:01.680 --> 15:05.960
It'll all be over before the duke's 
reinforcements ever arrive.

15:07.290 --> 15:12.410
I can already imagine the 
despair on Hubarek's face!

15:13.910 --> 15:18.140
<b>Margravate of Hubarek  Near Border</b>

15:18.750 --> 15:21.450
<i>I didn't expect my first 
deployment so suddenly.</i>

15:24.720 --> 15:26.350
<i>Take this to protect you.</i>

15:27.130 --> 15:28.970
<i>I can't afford to lose.</i>

15:29.650 --> 15:31.530
<i>I will protect Petra!</i>

15:38.700 --> 15:42.170
<b>The Day Before • Margravate of Hubarek</b>

15:40.420 --> 15:44.160
Well, if it isn't Lord Morteln and Lord Pastry!

15:44.890 --> 15:48.330
We heard you were under attack 
and wished to offer our aid.

15:48.680 --> 15:52.550
I'm truly grateful for this aid from afar.

15:52.550 --> 15:54.240
No, we're doing it for the goats!

15:54.240 --> 15:54.950
Hey!

15:56.530 --> 15:57.720
Goats?

15:57.720 --> 15:59.850
N-Nothing!

15:59.850 --> 16:03.690
I mean, anything to aid the 
family of my precious fiancée!

16:06.150 --> 16:07.580
How's the battle going?

16:07.580 --> 16:10.020
It's well for now.

16:10.860 --> 16:13.810
The enemy force isn't as large as I expected.

16:13.810 --> 16:17.470
They're preparing a strike from 
their front line fortress now.

16:18.120 --> 16:19.790
It's not that large?

16:19.790 --> 16:23.680
Yes, I thought they could be 30,000 strong,

16:23.680 --> 16:25.910
but in fact, it's closer to 12,000.

16:26.580 --> 16:28.500
I'd like to get your opinion, sir.

16:28.500 --> 16:30.100
Where are they set up?

16:30.460 --> 16:32.580
There are two thousand here.

16:32.580 --> 16:36.810
Their main force is here, with what 
looks like 500 provisionals nearby.

16:37.140 --> 16:40.270
We've got 200 of our men 
protecting this hill,

16:40.890 --> 16:43.750
and there are enemy forces here as well.

16:44.580 --> 16:46.840
<i>I see. Solid defenses.</i>

16:46.840 --> 16:48.060
It's curious.

16:48.060 --> 16:49.110
Curious?

16:49.490 --> 16:52.620
Something's not right. It doesn't add up.

16:52.620 --> 16:55.930
It all looks fine at a glance, but...

16:57.630 --> 16:59.990
You think so too?

16:59.990 --> 17:02.950
<i>A warrior's instinct?</i>

17:03.210 --> 17:08.240
<i>But for a veteran like Father, 
it's probably trustworthy.</i>

17:08.920 --> 17:13.630
But the formation certainly 
seems sensible and solid.

17:14.240 --> 17:15.900
What is it that doesn't feel right?

17:17.560 --> 17:19.440
Maybe it's too solid?

17:20.180 --> 17:21.310
What do you mean?

17:21.590 --> 17:24.520
It shouldn't be this solid, right?

17:24.830 --> 17:28.770
This is the formation of an army 
preparing for an attack from <i>us</i>.

17:29.420 --> 17:31.380
They're the ones invading,

17:32.380 --> 17:35.950
so why are they in a defensive formation?

17:36.200 --> 17:39.290
Yes, why would invaders 
reinforce their defenses

17:39.290 --> 17:42.330
before even a single battle's been fought?

17:42.910 --> 17:45.480
So that's what felt wrong about it.

17:45.480 --> 17:48.130
What are they after, then?

17:48.460 --> 17:50.790
You think they want to wear us down?

17:51.100 --> 17:53.880
No. If I were them...

17:55.370 --> 17:57.840
I'd leave the majority of my 
forces to solidify our defenses

17:58.090 --> 18:00.060
and make up for my lack of numbers

18:00.060 --> 18:04.470
by fighting a limited war 
with small mobile units,

18:04.990 --> 18:09.240
to slowly but surely shave down my 
opponent's numbers through repeated ambushes.

18:10.040 --> 18:11.530
Here, for instance.

18:12.170 --> 18:15.160
This is where I'd strike first.

18:16.640 --> 18:18.570
<i>If you put yourself in 
your opponent's position,</i>

18:18.570 --> 18:21.130
<i>you can figure out exactly 
what they're after?</i>

18:21.800 --> 18:25.590
If I'm assuming you're defending 
against attacks from the north,

18:25.590 --> 18:27.580
a strike here should leave me unscathed.

18:27.580 --> 18:29.770
The terrain also makes 
it perfect for an ambush.

18:32.630 --> 18:33.390
Sir?

18:34.210 --> 18:35.410
That's...

18:36.280 --> 18:39.840
That's where Lord Squale's unit is headed!

18:40.600 --> 18:42.050
Lord Squale?!

18:42.970 --> 18:45.880
I thought it would be an easy area to defend,

18:46.250 --> 18:49.020
and that it would be a good 
first deployment for him.

18:49.280 --> 18:51.740
Lord Squale has no combat experience.

18:51.740 --> 18:54.410
He won't last long as 
the target of an ambush!

18:54.410 --> 18:56.260
We must lend him our aid!

18:56.260 --> 18:57.450
You're right.

18:57.450 --> 18:59.740
I'll leave a company in your hands!

18:59.960 --> 19:01.890
Get to Lord Squale at once!

19:01.890 --> 19:02.980
Let's hurry, Pas!

19:02.980 --> 19:03.750
Right!

19:05.340 --> 19:07.100
Where do we expect the enemy to attack from?

19:07.100 --> 19:09.200
The northeast, we believe.

19:09.200 --> 19:10.210
Good.

19:10.210 --> 19:12.340
We'll meet them here and wipe them out!

19:12.340 --> 19:13.050
Sir!

19:13.940 --> 19:15.030
Excuse me, sir!

19:15.650 --> 19:17.580
We've sighted the enemy in the distance!

19:17.580 --> 19:18.660
About twenty men!

19:19.720 --> 19:20.690
It's time, then.

19:21.280 --> 19:22.240
Let's begin!

19:30.390 --> 19:32.890
<i>Where are they? Where is the enemy?!</i>

19:32.890 --> 19:34.360
It's an ambush!

19:34.360 --> 19:35.530
It's the enemy!

19:35.530 --> 19:37.320
It's an ambush from the southern forest!

19:37.320 --> 19:38.150
What?

19:38.150 --> 19:39.680
How did they get behind us?!

19:40.830 --> 19:43.280
Get them!

19:43.590 --> 19:45.740
Go!

19:46.420 --> 19:47.700
There are so many!

19:47.910 --> 19:50.410
I thought there were only twenty of them!

19:49.290 --> 19:50.970
Don't retreat! Meet them here!

19:50.970 --> 19:52.370
<i>They tricked us?</i>

19:58.330 --> 20:01.150
<i>Stay calm. Stay calm!</i>

20:02.110 --> 20:03.530
Lord Squale!

20:04.470 --> 20:06.180
Lord Squale, your orders?!

20:07.450 --> 20:08.840
We're playing into their hands here.

20:08.840 --> 20:09.680
Get into the forest!

20:09.680 --> 20:10.140
Sir!

20:17.520 --> 20:19.240
Enemy reinforcements! About a hundred!

20:19.240 --> 20:20.740
Lord Squale, your orders?!

20:21.230 --> 20:22.650
<i>We're trapped!</i>

20:29.620 --> 20:33.830
My lord, Margrave Hubarek's 
company is delayed!

20:33.830 --> 20:35.170
No time to wait for them!

20:35.170 --> 20:37.680
Nicolo, I'm leaving Hubarek's company to you!

20:37.680 --> 20:38.690
Yes, sir!

20:39.810 --> 20:43.700
Once we near the border, Pas, you take 
the soldiers and harangue the enemy!

20:43.700 --> 20:44.260
Sir!

20:44.260 --> 20:46.440
Glacage, you're with me!

20:46.440 --> 20:46.970
Sir!

20:47.540 --> 20:49.120
<i>Lord Squale...</i>

20:52.180 --> 20:53.830
Stay together! Don't disperse!

20:53.830 --> 20:55.270
That kid's their leader!

20:55.270 --> 20:56.670
Take him down!

20:56.670 --> 20:58.770
We need to retreat! All forces, fall back!

20:58.770 --> 20:59.860
We can't!

20:59.860 --> 21:01.820
They have us surrounded!

21:13.860 --> 21:15.330
We'll carve a path through.

21:15.330 --> 21:17.320
But we don't have enough men!

21:17.320 --> 21:18.790
We'd better surrender.

21:18.790 --> 21:20.510
We need to stay strong!

21:25.280 --> 21:26.810
Wh-What is...

21:38.660 --> 21:41.270
Is that... Lord Morteln?

21:44.250 --> 21:47.420
What's Lord Morteln doing here?

21:47.420 --> 21:50.010
I'm glad you're safe, Lord Squale!

21:52.080 --> 21:53.400
It's been a while.

21:53.400 --> 21:56.690
We heard about your first deployment 
and came to lend a hand!

23:36.970 --> 23:39.180
Next time on <i>Sweet Reincarnation</i>:

23:39.080 --> 23:44.940
<b>The Flavor of Consolation: Tarte Tatin</b>

23:39.180 --> 23:41.830
"The Flavor of Consolation: Tarte Tatin"

23:41.830 --> 23:43.190
Bon appétit!

23:44.940 --> 23:50.250
<b>Illustration:</b>

23:44.940 --> 23:50.250
<b>Kaito Shibano</b>
